Overlay patch 0051: run ImGui in POINT space on iOS/visionOS, matching
EVERY other HarbourMasters port (SoH, 2ship, Starship, Spaghetti). THE fix
for "the menu is far too small, no other port had to mess with this."

This fork's newer LUS is the lone outlier: it forces the whole UI into
DRAWABLE-PIXEL space in two places, so ImGui lays the menu out in ~2736 px
where the shared shell (built for point space) and the Ship of Harkinian port 0015 both
assume ~912 pt — hence a menu ~3x too small that needed compensation hacks.
Verified by reading all three sibling forks: their GfxWindowBackendSDL2::
GetDimensions uses SDL_GetWindowSize (points) and their Fast3dGui does NOT
override io.DisplaySize. This patch makes Ghostship do the same:

1. GetDimensions -> SDL_GetWindowSize (points) on __APPLE__, so wnd->
   GetWidth() — which sizes the "Main - Deck" and "Main Game" windows — is
   in points, exactly like the Ship of Harkinian port (gfx_sdl2.cpp:540) and 2ship (:522).
2. Remove the Fast3dGui pixel-space override so io.DisplaySize stays the
   point-space value ImGui_ImplSDL2_NewFrame set.

Why this is safe where the earlier half-fix (retired 0049) was not: 0049
changed ONLY DisplaySize and left GetDimensions returning pixels, so the
deck window (GetWidth=2736) was 3x oversized in a 912-pt space and the game
drew 2x too big. Changing BOTH makes everything point-consistent — the game
image is a point-space quad that overlay 0010 upscales to the drawable
(FramebufferScale = drawable/DisplaySize), and overlay 0032's SSAA scales
mCurDimensions from the point content region up to native px, which is what
0032's own comment always described. Same design the three siblings run.

Deletes the entire compensation apparatus (0015 rev5/6, 0050, shell D13/D14)
in one stroke: at point space a plain 0.85 is the right size.

